  "scope_limits": [
    "The original case remains failed. A successful one-shot fault and dedicated exit7 do not turn failed explicit product recovery into a pass.",
    "Journal receipt latency is not FPGA-to-process latency, an exact exit timestamp or a worst-case bound; native terminal status was not sampled while the desktop was paused.",
    "Manual basic USB receiver creation was needed on the old runtime. Its first observer used the wrong slice key and failed after creation; a separate read verified the existing slice and selected USB without creating another receiver.",
    "The fix is host-tested only. No updated runtime, live fixed recovery, keyed DSP API fault, production release or actual6300 qualification is claimed.",
    "In this receive-only case native exit7 survived the diagnostic wrapper. Before a future keyed API-loss case, preserve exit7 explicitly in the diagnostic finalizer or use the uninstrumented runtime; a keyed non-READY completion can currently exit2.",
    "pidfd_getfd is a bench-only8600 injection mechanism, not a Linux2.6 product requirement. All private receiver-state, compiler caches, vault contents and private keys are excluded.",
    "Cold-start bypass, historical natural128sample cause and the full P1-P10 delivery/qualification scope remain open."
  ],
  "next_step": "Build the exact fixed full ARMv7/ARM64 runtime reproducibly, verify changed components and disk bounds, then use the ordinary approved upgrade. Dispatch a new receive-only DSP API fault with fresh ownership witness, allow READY/RECEIVE only after the unkeyed fault, and prove explicit Restore receive plus fresh USB DAX IQ successor and exact cleanup. Preserve the old failed run; no automatic RF retry/rearm or software reboot."
